---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import company from '../data/company.json';
---

<Layout
  title="Terms & Conditions | Iconic Travel & Tours (GL #5247)"
  description="Booking conditions, cancellation terms, visa responsibilities, and travel policies for Iconic Travel & Tours (GL #5247)."
>

  <section class="py-16 bg-brand-emerald text-white">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 text-center space-y-3">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-[0.25em] text-brand-gold">Booking Agreement</span>
      <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-bold">Terms & Conditions</h1>
      <p class="text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-ivory/80">Draft Booking Policy — Subject to client and legal review</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-16 bg-brand-ivory">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 bg-white p-8 sm:p-12 rounded-3xl border border-brand-gold/25 shadow-sm space-y-8 text-xs sm:text-sm text-brand-charcoal-light leading-relaxed">
      
      <div class="p-4 rounded-xl bg-amber-50 border border-amber-200 text-amber-900 text-xs">
        <strong>Client Review Notice:</strong> This document serves as an editable operational booking template for Iconic Travel & Tours (GL #5247). Final commercial agreements may vary based on seasonal airline contracts and hotel block booking clauses.
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-brand-emerald">1. Booking Confirmation & Deposits</h2>
        <p>
          A booking is deemed confirmed only upon receipt of the designated booking advance and issuance of an official computerized receipt bearing Government License GL #5247. The remaining balance must be cleared prior to ticket issuance and visa processing according to the agreed schedule.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-brand-emerald">2. Pricing & Currency Fluctuations</h2>
        <p>
          Quoted prices are based on prevailing hotel tariffs, airline net fares, and foreign currency exchange rates (SAR/PKR). In the event of statutory increases in Saudi municipality taxes, VAT, visa levies, or substantial currency devaluations, Iconic Travel & Tours reserves the right to adjust package pricing transparently with documented notice.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-brand-emerald">3. Saudi Visa & Regulatory Authority</h2>
        <p>
          While Iconic Travel & Tours acts as an authorized processing facilitator under GL #5247, the grant, rejection, delay, or conditions of entry visas remain the sole sovereign prerogative of the Ministry of Hajj & Umrah and the Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-brand-emerald">4. Accommodation & Room Occupancy</h2>
        <p>
          Hotel check-in and check-out timings conform to standard Saudi hospitality norms (typically check-in at 04:00 PM and check-out at 12:00 PM). Sharing configurations (Quad, Triple, Double) represent the number of registered occupants per room. Room allocations are made in good faith with equivalent or superior properties if unforeseen hotel operational constraints arise.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-brand-emerald">5. Group Travel & Punctuality Protocol</h2>
        <p>
          Pilgrims participating in organized group tours (e.g. TECNO Umrah Group Tour) agree to adhere to instructions given by the designated group coordinator, maintain punctuality for coach departures, respect fellow travelers, and observe breakfast hall hours (06:30 AM – 10:00 AM).
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-brand-emerald">6. Cancellations & Refunds</h2>
        <p>
          Cancellations requested after visa issuance, ticket stamping, or hotel voucher generation are governed by the penalty schedules of the respective airlines and Saudi hotel operators. Administrative processing fees are non-refundable.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="space-y-3">
        <h2 class="font-serif text-xl font-bold text-brand-emerald">7. Governing Law & Dispute Resolution</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of the Islamic Republic of Pakistan and tourist regulations under the Department of Tourist Services (GL #5247). Any dispute shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the courts of Karachi, Pakistan.
        </p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Layout>
